---
import '../styles/global.css'
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>MDTASK | Your AI agent's backlog lives in your files</title>
    <meta name="description" content="A CLI task manager where Markdown checkboxes in your PRDs and READMEs are the backlog. You and your AI coding agent edit the same lines — no second tracker, nothing to sync. Spec-driven development without the drift." />

    <!-- Open Graph / Facebook -->
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="MDTASK | Your AI agent's backlog lives in your files" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Markdown checkboxes in your PRDs and READMEs are the backlog. You and your AI agent edit the same lines. No second tracker, nothing to sync." />

    <!-- Twitter -->
    <meta property="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <meta property="twitter:title" content="MDTASK | Your AI agent's backlog lives in your files" />
    <meta property="twitter:description" content="Markdown checkboxes in your PRDs and READMEs are the backlog. You and your AI agent edit the same lines. No second tracker, nothing to sync." />

    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
    <style>
      body { font-family: 'Space Grotesk', monospace; }
      pre, code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body class="bg-background text-on-background selection:bg-secondary-container antialiased">
    <!-- Announcement Banner -->
    <div class="bg-surface-container-high text-on-background px-6 py-2 text-center text-xs font-medium border-b border-surface-container">
      <span class="bg-tertiary-container text-on-tertiary-container px-2 py-0.5 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[0.6rem] mr-2">Beta</span>
      Early version. <a href="https://github.com/syabro/mdtask/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="underline decoration-on-surface-variant/40 hover:text-on-background hover:decoration-on-background transition-colors">Issues and ideas are very welcome.</a>
    </div>

    <!-- Nav -->
    <nav class="w-full bg-background flex justify-between items-center px-6 py-4 max-w-full mx-auto border-b border-surface-container">
      <div class="text-lg font-bold tracking-tighter text-on-background">MDTASK</div>
      <div class="hidden md:flex gap-8 items-center">
        <a class="font-body uppercase tracking-[0.05em] text-[0.6875rem] text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-background transition-colors" href="#proof">Proof</a>
        <a class="font-body uppercase tracking-[0.05em] text-[0.6875rem] text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-background transition-colors" href="#how">How it works</a>
        <a class="font-body uppercase tracking-[0.05em] text-[0.6875rem] text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-background transition-colors" href="#compare">Compare</a>
        <a class="font-body uppercase tracking-[0.05em] text-[0.6875rem] text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-background transition-colors" href="#faq">FAQ</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <main>
      <!-- Hero -->
      <section class="px-6 md:px-24 py-12 md:py-24 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-start">
        <div class="flex flex-col">
          <span class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold text-tertiary block mb-5">Spec-Driven Development</span>
          <h1 class="text-[2.25rem] md:text-[2.75rem] leading-[1.1] font-bold tracking-tight text-on-background mb-8">
            Your AI agent's backlog lives in your Markdown files
          </h1>
          <div class="space-y-4 mb-16">
            <p class="text-on-background text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
              Tasks are checkboxes in the PRDs and READMEs you already have. You and your coding agent read and edit the exact same lines — no second tracker, no API, nothing to sync.
            </p>
            <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-base max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
              Your agent picks them up once you drop in the mdtask skill.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 items-stretch w-full lg:max-w-xl">
            <div id="copy-install" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Copy install command" title="Copy" class="bg-surface-container flex-1 flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 group cursor-pointer transition-shadow">
              <code class="text-[0.875rem] text-on-surface font-medium whitespace-nowrap overflow-hidden text-ellipsis">npm install -g mdtask</code>
              <svg class="ml-4 w-4 h-4 opacity-60 group-hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity shrink-0 fill-current text-on-surface" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <path d="M16 1H4c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v14h2V3h12V1zm3 4H8c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v14c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h11c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V7c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2zm0 16H8V7h11v14z"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <a href="https://github.com/syabro/mdtask" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-[#312e2c] text-surface px-6 py-3 text-[0.6875rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest hover:bg-primary active:translate-y-[1px] transition-all whitespace-nowrap border-b-2 border-transparent">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 fill-current" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <path d="M12 .297c-6.63 0-12 5.373-12 12 0 5.303 3.438 9.8 8.205 11.385.6.113.82-.258.82-.577 0-.285-.01-1.04-.015-2.04-3.338.724-4.042-1.61-4.042-1.61C4.422 18.07 3.633 17.7 3.633 17.7c-1.087-.744.084-.729.084-.729 1.205.084 1.838 1.236 1.838 1.236 1.07 1.835 2.809 1.305 3.495.998.108-.776.417-1.305.76-1.605-2.665-.3-5.466-1.332-5.466-5.93 0-1.31.465-2.38 1.235-3.22-.135-.303-.54-1.523.105-3.176 0 0 1.005-.322 3.3 1.23.96-.267 1.98-.399 3-.405 1.02.006 2.04.138 3 .405 2.28-1.552 3.285-1.23 3.285-1.23.645 1.653.24 2.873.12 3.176.765.84 1.23 1.91 1.23 3.22 0 4.61-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.92.43.372.823 1.102.823 2.222 0 1.606-.015 2.896-.015 3.286 0 .315.21.69.825.57C20.565 22.092 24 17.592 24 12.297c0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12"/>
              </svg>
              View on GitHub
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 border-l-4 border-tertiary shadow-2xl overflow-hidden text-[0.65rem] sm:text-[0.7rem] md:text-[0.8125rem]">
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-4">
            <span class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-widest font-bold opacity-40">docs/prd/deploy.md</span>
          </div>
          <pre class="text-on-background leading-loose"># Deploy pipeline
- [x] DEP-001 Containerize the API
- [ ] DEP-002 Blue-green rollout      <span class="text-error">!high</span>
- [ ] DEP-003 Rollback command        <span class="text-secondary">@blocked_by:DEP-002</span>
- [ ] DEP-004 Smoke-test on deploy     <span class="text-error">!high</span> <span class="text-secondary">#ci</span></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Proof: one file, two views -->
      <section class="bg-surface-container-high py-20 md:py-32 px-6 md:px-24" id="proof">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
          <div class="mb-12 md:mb-16">
            <span class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold text-tertiary block mb-4">// 01. PROOF</span>
            <h2 class="text-[2.5rem] font-bold tracking-tight mb-6">One file. Two views.</h2>
            <p class="text-lg text-on-background leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
              The open checkboxes in your spec are the list your agent works from. There is no sync step, because there is no second copy. mdtask is built this way — its own backlog is a set of Markdown files in its repo.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 items-stretch">
            <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 border border-outline-variant overflow-hidden text-[0.62rem] sm:text-[0.7rem] md:text-[0.8125rem]">
              <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-4">
                <span class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-widest font-bold opacity-40">docs/prd/search.md</span>
                <span class="text-[0.6rem] uppercase tracking-widest text-tertiary">the spec</span>
              </div>
              <pre class="text-on-background leading-loose">## Tasks
- [x] SRCH-001 Basic CLI parser
      <span class="opacity-50">**Implemented:** ripgrep scan, 0 deps</span>
- [ ] SRCH-002 Priority filtering   <span class="text-error">!high</span>
- [ ] SRCH-003 Git-hook integration <span class="text-secondary">@iter:mvp</span>
- [ ] SRCH-004 Documentation sweep  <span class="text-secondary">#docs</span></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="terminal p-6 text-[0.62rem] sm:text-[0.7rem] md:text-[0.8125rem] overflow-hidden">
              <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-4 border-b border-surface-variant/10 pb-2">
                <span class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-widest text-surface/40">Terminal</span>
                <span class="text-[0.6rem] uppercase tracking-widest text-tertiary-fixed-dim">the backlog</span>
              </div>
              <pre class="leading-loose"><span class="text-surface/30 select-none mr-2">$</span><span class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim font-bold">mdtask list</span>
<span class="text-surface/60">[ ]</span> <span class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim">SRCH-002</span> <span class="text-surface/80">Priority filtering</span>     <span class="text-error">!high</span>
<span class="text-surface/60">[ ]</span> <span class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim">SRCH-003</span> <span class="text-surface/80">Git-hook integration</span>   <span class="text-secondary-fixed-dim">@iter:mvp</span>
<span class="text-surface/60">[ ]</span> <span class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim">SRCH-004</span> <span class="text-surface/80">Documentation sweep</span>    <span class="text-secondary-fixed-dim">#docs</span>
<span class="text-surface/40">3 tasks pending.</span></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm mt-5 leading-relaxed">
            <span class="text-on-background font-medium">SRCH-001</span> is checked off in the spec, so it is gone from the list. Same lines, no database.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- How it works -->
      <section class="py-20 md:py-32 px-6 md:px-24 border-t border-surface-container" id="how">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <div class="mb-12 md:mb-16">
            <span class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold text-tertiary block mb-4">// 02. HOW IT WORKS</span>
            <h2 class="text-[2.5rem] font-bold tracking-tight">It's just Markdown.</h2>
          </div>

          <!-- Beat 1: a task is one line -->
          <div class="mb-14">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold mb-4 uppercase tracking-widest text-tertiary">Looks like a checkbox — carries an ID, priority, and tags</h3>
            <div class="relative bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 md:p-8 overflow-hidden border border-outline-variant">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-on-background text-[0.65rem] sm:text-xs md:text-base mb-6">
                <span class="font-mono">- [ ]</span>
                <span class="font-mono bg-tertiary-container text-on-tertiary-container px-1">CLI-042</span>
                <span class="font-mono">Add export command</span>
                <span class="font-mono text-secondary">#cli</span>
                <span class="font-mono text-error">!high</span>
                <span class="font-mono text-on-surface-variant">@status:in-progress</span>
              </div>
              <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-6 gap-y-6 gap-x-6 pt-5 border-t border-surface-container items-start">
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
                  <p class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase font-bold text-outline">Status</p>
                  <div class="font-mono text-sm leading-none">[ ]</div>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
                  <p class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase font-bold text-outline">ID</p>
                  <div><span class="font-mono text-sm leading-none bg-tertiary-container text-on-tertiary-container px-1 inline-block">CLI-042</span></div>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
                  <p class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase font-bold text-outline">Title</p>
                  <div class="font-mono text-sm leading-none">Add export command</div>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
                  <p class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase font-bold text-outline">Tag</p>
                  <div class="font-mono text-sm leading-none text-secondary">#cli</div>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
                  <p class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase font-bold text-outline">Priority</p>
                  <div class="font-mono text-sm leading-none text-error">!high</div>
                </div>
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
                  <p class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase font-bold text-outline">Property</p>
                  <div class="font-mono text-sm leading-none text-on-surface-variant">@status:in-progress</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed">The checkbox line holds the ID, title, and metadata. Longer notes — the spec, an <code class="text-on-background">**Implemented:**</code> block — just indent underneath. Standard Markdown: write it by hand, read it in any editor, parse it with grep.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Beat 2: your agent works the backlog -->
          <div class="mb-14">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold mb-4 uppercase tracking-widest text-tertiary">Your agent picks a task, ships it, and checks it off</h3>
            <div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 border border-outline-variant overflow-hidden mb-4 text-[0.7rem] md:text-[0.8125rem]">
              <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-3">
                <span class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-widest font-bold opacity-40">docs/prd/deploy.md</span>
                <span class="text-[0.6rem] uppercase tracking-widest text-tertiary">before → after</span>
              </div>
              <pre class="leading-loose text-on-background"><span class="opacity-40">- [ ] DEP-002 Blue-green rollout      !high</span>

- [x] DEP-002 Blue-green rollout      <span class="text-error">!high</span>
      <span class="opacity-60">**Implemented:** ALB target-group swap, zero downtime</span></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">Your coding agent reads the open task, does the work, then flips it to <code class="text-on-background">[x]</code> and writes what it did — into the file, not a separate status field. One-time setup: <code class="text-on-background">mdtask install-skills</code> teaches Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex the convention.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Beat 3: query across every file -->
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold mb-4 uppercase tracking-widest text-tertiary">Query across every file</h3>
            <div class="terminal p-6 text-[0.7rem] md:text-[0.8125rem] overflow-hidden mb-4">
              <pre class="leading-loose"><span class="text-surface/30 select-none mr-2">$</span><span class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim font-bold">mdtask list --tag ci --priority high</span>
<span class="text-surface/60">[ ]</span> <span class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim">DEP-004</span> <span class="text-surface/80">Smoke-test on deploy</span>  <span class="text-error">!high</span>  <span class="text-secondary-fixed-dim">#ci</span></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="text-on-surface-variant text-sm leading-relaxed">Scattered across READMEs and PRDs, your checkboxes become one queryable backlog. Filter by tag or priority, flag blockers with <code class="text-on-background">@blocked_by</code>, check integrity with <code class="text-on-background">validate</code>, and auto-assign IDs to existing checkboxes with <code class="text-on-background">ids</code>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Compare -->
      <section class="bg-on-background text-surface py-20 md:py-32 px-6 md:px-24" id="compare">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <div class="mb-12 md:mb-16">
            <span class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold text-tertiary-fixed-dim block mb-4">// 03. INSTEAD OF</span>
            <h2 class="text-[2rem] font-bold tracking-tight">You already have the alternatives. Here's the trade.</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col divide-y divide-surface/10">
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[180px_1fr] gap-2 md:gap-8 py-7">
              <div class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest">Spec Kit / Kiro</div>
              <div class="text-surface/80 leading-relaxed">They generate a spec, then a separate plan that drifts the moment code lands. mdtask makes your spec's own checkboxes the backlog — tick one off and the spec and the work stay the same lines.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[180px_1fr] gap-2 md:gap-8 py-7">
              <div class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest">TODO.md</div>
              <div class="text-surface/80 leading-relaxed">Same instinct, no structure. mdtask adds stable IDs you can reference, cross-file queries, and blockers you can flag — and an agent that reads and ticks them off. Still plain Markdown.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[180px_1fr] gap-2 md:gap-8 py-7">
              <div class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest">Linear / Jira</div>
              <div class="text-surface/80 leading-relaxed">
                Built without either. For solo and small-team dev with an agent, the Markdown <em>is</em> the tracker — no SaaS, no seats, no sync.
                <span class="block text-surface/40 text-sm mt-2">Need org-wide sprints and stakeholder dashboards? That part is still Linear's.</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[180px_1fr] gap-2 md:gap-8 py-7">
              <div class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest">Obsidian / Logseq</div>
              <div class="text-surface/80 leading-relaxed">Not a competitor — it's the same files. Because tasks are plain Markdown, they show up in your notes app too. mdtask just adds a CLI your agent and your scripts can drive.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- FAQ -->
      <section class="py-20 md:py-32 px-6 md:px-24" id="faq">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          <div class="mb-12 md:mb-20 text-center">
            <span class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold text-tertiary block mb-4">// 04. FREQUENTLY ASKED</span>
            <h2 class="text-[2.5rem] font-bold tracking-tight">Got questions?</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-12">
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <p class="font-bold text-lg">Isn't this just a TODO.md?</p>
              <p class="text-on-background leading-relaxed">Almost — and that's the point. The difference is stable IDs you can reference, queries across every file (<code class="text-on-surface-variant">mdtask list --tag deploy</code>), blockers you can flag, and a format your AI agent already understands. Still plain Markdown you can edit by hand.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <p class="font-bold text-lg">What about git merge conflicts?</p>
              <p class="text-on-background leading-relaxed">They're ordinary text conflicts — two people changed lines in the same Markdown file. You resolve them in git like any other line. There's no hidden state and no special tooling; we don't pretend git auto-merges them for you.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <p class="font-bold text-lg">Does my agent need setup?</p>
              <p class="text-on-background leading-relaxed">Run <code class="text-on-surface-variant">mdtask install-skills</code> once to drop the skill into your agent's folder. After that Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex read and update tasks in the same files you do. Without it, a plain agent can still read the checkboxes — it just won't follow the conventions.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <p class="font-bold text-lg">What if I outgrow it?</p>
              <p class="text-on-background leading-relaxed">It's plain Markdown in your repo, so there's nothing to export and no lock-in. Keep it alongside Linear or Jira for the work that hasn't become a team ticket yet, or move on entirely — your tasks stay readable either way.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- CTA Section -->
      <section class="bg-surface-container-high py-20 md:py-32 px-6 md:px-24 border-t border-surface-container">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-12 md:gap-16 items-center">
          <div class="flex-1 space-y-6">
            <h2 class="text-[2.5rem] leading-[1.1] font-bold tracking-tight text-on-background">Point it at the files you already have</h2>
            <p class="text-lg text-on-background leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
              Run <code class="text-on-surface-variant">mdtask ids</code> in any repo with Markdown. It finds your existing checkboxes and offers to give them IDs — your backlog, already there.
            </p>
            <div class="pt-4">
              <a href="https://github.com/syabro/mdtask" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-[#312e2c] text-surface px-8 py-4 text-[0.6875rem] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest hover:bg-primary active:translate-y-[1px] transition-all">
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 fill-current" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M12 .297c-6.63 0-12 5.373-12 12 0 5.303 3.438 9.8 8.205 11.385.6.113.82-.258.82-.577 0-.285-.01-1.04-.015-2.04-3.338.724-4.042-1.61-4.042-1.61C4.422 18.07 3.633 17.7 3.633 17.7c-1.087-.744.084-.729.084-.729 1.205.084 1.838 1.236 1.838 1.236 1.07 1.835 2.809 1.305 3.495.998.108-.776.417-1.305.76-1.605-2.665-.3-5.466-1.332-5.466-5.93 0-1.31.465-2.38 1.235-3.22-.135-.303-.54-1.523.105-3.176 0 0 1.005-.322 3.3 1.23.96-.267 1.98-.399 3-.405 1.02.006 2.04.138 3 .405 2.28-1.552 3.285-1.23 3.285-1.23.645 1.653.24 2.873.12 3.176.765.84 1.23 1.91 1.23 3.22 0 4.61-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.92.43.372.823 1.102.823 2.222 0 1.606-.015 2.896-.015 3.286 0 .315.21.69.825.57C20.565 22.092 24 17.592 24 12.297c0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12"/></svg>
                View on GitHub
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal w-full md:w-[480px] md:min-h-[160px] p-6 text-sm flex-shrink-0 flex flex-col">
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-4 border-b border-surface-variant/10 pb-2 shrink-0">
              <span class="text-[0.6875rem] uppercase tracking-widest text-surface/40">Terminal</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="leading-loose"><span class="text-surface/30 select-none mr-2">$</span><span class="text-tertiary-fixed-dim font-bold">cd my-project &amp;&amp; npx mdtask ids</span>
<span class="text-surface/60">Enter prefix for README.md: </span><span class="text-surface">KTL</span>
